## AUDIT LAW 1: ZERO-TRUST VERIFICATION
#   - Never trust claims like "Ready for production" or "All tests pass"
#     without proof. Every file path, function call, storage key, and status
#     transition must be cross-checked line-by-line against actual code.
#   - ADDITION: Cross-check all findings against existing .windsurfrules laws
#     (Saga Law, Tier Law, Domain Law) before raising new gaps.

## AUDIT LAW 2: 70/30 EDGE-CASE FOCUS
#   - 70% of analysis: failure modes, network drops, stale localStorage/cookies,
#     race conditions, expired tokens, silent error handling.
#   - 30% of analysis: happy paths.

## AUDIT LAW 3: STRICT ERROR & LOGGING AUDIT
#   - Reject: empty catch blocks, unhandled promise rejections, missing fallbacks,
#     infinite UI retry loops.
#   - Enforce: explicit error classifications (Terminal vs Soft Error) with
#     actionable user pathways.

## AUDIT LAW 4: QA & AUTOMATION ENFORCEMENT
#   - Architecture is "Unfinished" until a corresponding automated E2E test suite
#     (Playwright/Cypress) is explicitly mapped.
#   - SQL smoke tests or unit tests are NOT sufficient for E2E validation.

## AUDIT LAW 5: DECISIVE ACTIONABLE OUTPUTS
